Subject: Keep the complete matrix-handle chain pointer-sized on native hosts

Upstream-base: 11c0bc65ad2ec21431c5d74f1ac4cbc1e3e2e2c3

Matrix handles address live GL matrix storage. Preserve their width through
allocation, global state, model packets, draw/text callers, render caches and
shadow-lighting hooks; keep console typedefs and serialized u32 indices intact.
Select the original matrix access/model propagation without material/display-list
methods. Native access validates aligned, active-frame or live-resource ranges
before dereferencing, and ordered memory shutdown resets the identity handle.
A range check does not give handles unique identities after address reuse.
Unselected loaders/materials and missing lighting globals still require their
own integration; widened declarations do not make those units linkable.

